        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "H4L (42.5 mg, 0.05 mmol) and Gd(OAc)3·4H2O (40.0 mg, 0.1 mmol) in EtOH/CHCl3 (1:1 v/v, 20 mL) were refluxed for 15 min. The solution was evaporated to dryness and the white residue was recrystallized from the same solvent to give colorless blocks of 1·8EtOH·4H2O over several days (87%). The body text specifies the gadolinium acetate tetrahydrate; the experimental line is OCR-ambiguous as ·3H2O but the stated mass matches about 0.1 mmol of the tetrahydrate.",
